  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:14 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Edwin S. Kneedler, Deputy Solicitor General)",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Exactly when did it do this? What's the exact date?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BLATT: No. Remember, Solem was not on the books until 80 years after Oklahoma became a state."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What's so interesting -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ian H. Gershengorn (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Thomas's opinion in Parker from just three terms ago requires that the Tenth Circuit decision be affirmed. Parker confirmed that the text is what governs, and the text here is particularly clear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What happens to all those people? What happens to all those laws?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GERSHENGORN",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the state's concerns are dramatically overstated, but, in any event, this Court has doctrines designed to address it"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Muscogee (Creek) Nation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There will not be turmoil because of three reasons: One, this Court's precedents restrict tribal power over non-Indians on fee lands within reservations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, suppose an Indian is charged in -- with having committed a mugging in Tulsa. What -- where would that case end up?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Nine percent of -- of how many people?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: So, if any of those individuals was charged with any offense that would normally be prosecuted in state court, they would all have to be prosecuted in federal court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Creek Nation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Nation has a robust criminal jurisdiction, has robust courts, is already prosecuting many Indians."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Creek Nation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There already are discussions taking place here about the allocation of jurisdiction. Congress has provided mechanisms for the allocation of both criminal and civil jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, if we don't agree with you on that point, if we think this is a practical inquiry, can you tell me what sovereign powers the Nation retained within this territory after statehood?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0003-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Affirmance raises a specter of tearing families all across eastern Oklahoma, and probably beyond, for years and years and years and years after the fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e822f1390831c8d4a2868135baf3e0040f73861b12ef526bfb1733fb5ccc2f9b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e822f1390831-0003-0007",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Every tribal chief that we cited, every federal court, every tribal lawyer, members of Congress, every Oklahoma historian, and the popular press recognized -- and some of these are not racist, but they are the foremost Indian scholars at the time of Oklahoma -- that the tribal governments had ceased to function."
    },
